::kind(writ)

=[ Writ: dev-dependency fixture ]

==[ crate-layering ]

Dev-dependencies are exempt. A crate may reach upward in
`[dev-dependencies]` to get something to test itself against, because
that says nothing about how the shipped code is arranged.

@rule(crate-layering){
  guard: { twrit: layers }

  layers: {
    2: list("top")
    1: list("mid")
    0: list("base")
  }
}

This is `upward-edge` with the one edge moved to `[dev-dependencies]`.
Same layers, same direction, and nothing is reported.
